"bm_george|Ari rolled his right ankle and stretched a ligament. That is a mild sprain.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Most mild sprains heal in about 2 weeks. A brace or a walking boot protects the ankle while it heals.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|If Ari plays on Saturday wearing a brace, about 1 in 10 kids like him roll the ankle again, and with only tape, about 2 in 10 do.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Because Ari hides pain, I updated my forecast: if he plays on Saturday, about 3 in 10 kids like him roll the ankle again in a brace, and about 5 in 10 do with tape.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|A second sprain takes about 6 weeks to heal, which is three times as long as the first one.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|My forecast assumes Ari will stop playing when his ankle hurts. Most kids do stop, but not all of them.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Ari\u2019s grandma says he hides pain, so he might keep playing even when his ankle hurts.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
